# VM script-dialect case (legacy `test/vm/18_ffi/016_json_is_null`)

`.as` expression exercising script lowering through the production
path-carrying API. The legacy per-case wrapper is `#[ignore]`d (unwired);
this import makes the corpus piece observable again. The legacy expected file
said `1`, but it was NEVER verified (the wrapper is #[ignore]d):
`Json.is_null("null")` returns a bool, displayed as `true`. Oracle
corrected and recorded as `unwired-revived+corrected-oracle`.

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/1"
  id: "lang.script.json-is-null"
  tags: ["pilot", "vm", "as-script"]
  source: { file: "vm/18_ffi/016_json_is_null/json_is_null.as", syntax: "auto-script", path: "main.as" }
  entry: { mode: "expression" }
  checks: [
    { id: "vm", adapter: "avm", action: "run",
      expect: { completion: "success", result: { format: "legacy-display", text: "true" } } }
  ]
}
```
